<!DOCTYPE html>
<!-- Quantum HTML + CSS example 13_selectors/14: Combinators -->
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Combinators</title>
  <style>
    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.5;
      color: #1f2933;
      background: #f5f7fa;
    }
    .demo { max-width: 60rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.25rem; }
    .demo > h1 { margin: 0 0 0.25rem; font-size: 2rem; }
    .lead { margin: 0 0 2rem; color: #52606d; }

    .tree * { margin: 0.25rem 0; padding: 0.25rem 0.5rem; border-radius: 6px; }
    .tree p { background: #f1f5f9; }
    .child > p { outline: 2px solid #3b82f6; }
    h2 + p { background: #fde68a; }
    h2 ~ p { font-style: italic; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="demo">
    <h1>Combinators</h1>
    <p class="lead">Descendant, child, adjacent sibling and general sibling.</p>
    <div class="tree child">
      <h2>Heading</h2>
      <p>Adjacent to h2: yellow. A child of .child: blue outline.</p>
      <p>A later sibling of h2: italic.</p>
      <div><p>Nested deeper: a descendant, not a child.</p></div>
    </div>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
